{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1545066-alt-history-tremere-becomes-liches","id":1545066,"title":"Alt-history; Tremere becomes liches","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-30T13:14:58-07:00","id":1545066,"title":"Alt-history; Tremere becomes liches","content":"So as a mental exercise, what would have happened to the metaplots of VtM and MtA if the Tremere had become liches rather than vampires? <br /> Say at the leadership of House Tremere (Tremere himself and his six homies) becomes liches and using Vile Magic (tm) prolong the lives of their prefered servants. But they are caught and kicked out of the Order. So, the Tremere never hunt the Salubri, but hang around in the shadows occasionally harassing and hunting mages.<br /> <br /> What would the modern setting of VtM and MtA look like?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-30T16:00:08-07:00","id":1545076,"title":"","content":"As liches the Tremere wouldn't interact with vampire society other than maybe for a research project.<br /> <br /> Off the top of my head the VtM setting would change as follows:<br /> 1. Assamites would never have been cursed after being defeated, probably leading to the extinction of the clan or decimation down to a bloodline population.<br /> 2. Gargoyles would never have been created<br /> 3. Salubri would be a full sized clan with two internal factions<br /> 4. Most Elders would have ratings in Koldunic sorcery ways rather than random Thaumaturgy paths or perhaps no magic at all.<br /> 5. The Kuei-Jin invasion of the west coast would not be stopped since there would be no Tremere to ward them into a containment zone in San Francisco.<br /> 6. A successful Kuei-Jin invasion would mean the anarch movement on the west coast would have been crushed trying to fight a two front war.<br /> <br /> Without the Tremere being the upstarts and troublemakers that they were, there are a few things that while not directly connected to them, the existence of the Tremere may have pushed certain things into being or certain courses of action. But these are far more speculation than factual.<br /> <br /> 1. The creation of the Blood Brothers bloodline, inspired by the creation of the Gargoyles or as a counter to them probably wouldn't have happened.<br /> 2. The Salubri and Tzimisce were friendly clans and given the Salubris probability to join the Camarilla, it is possible that the Domain Lords would have joined rather than being part of the Sabbat, or at least the clan would have split with the Kolduns going to the Camarilla and the flesh crafters going to the Sabbat.<br /> 3. Without the Tremere stealing unlife for themselves, diablerizing an Antedeluvian, and holding their own against three other main clans, it is fair to wonder if the revolt that created the need for the Camarilla or the Sabbat would have even happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-30T16:05:58-07:00","id":1545078,"title":"","content":"Without Vitae/Vampirism in the mix, the Tremere never have a reason to hunt the Salubri. If anything, they're more likely to hunt other Clans with older Blood Sorcery traditions (Assamites, Setites, Cappadocians, etc) to steal their magical knowledge. The Salubri Antedeluvian, by contrast, has nothing to offer Tremere Liches, so neither he nor his Clan would even be on their radar. Not unless the Warrior Salubri decide the Liches are too vile and unholy to live, so <i>they</i> make <i>themselves</i> House Tremere's problem.<br /> <br /> Again, though, I don't see the Tremere wanting to exterminate the Salubri. The reason the Tremere slandered the Salubri and brought Blood Hunts against them is as a political move to keep the rest of Kindred society from turning on the obvious usurpers. The Warlocks turned from upstarts to active threats to Kindred society. Turning the blame on a weak, somewhat disliked Clan was their Refuge In Audacity. Even then, it only barely worked long enough for the Tremere to get in on the ground floor of the nascent Camarilla during the Anarch Revolt.<br /> <br /> If Diablerizing Saulot doesn't happen, neither does the political machinations meant to protect the Tremere. The Liches would just be a shadowy cabal of arcane rivals to existing Kindred in the immediate sense, little different from any others. Many Elders and Methuselahs would barely notice the undead wizards were even around, if at all.<br /> <br /> Circling back around to the Anarch Revolt, I imagine that still happens, as does the rise of the Camarilla. If only because if the Tremere weren't there, someone else would have to do the political heavy lifting of forging the alliance. And I trust that the Ventrue have that task well in hand.<br /> <br /> What I definitely see playing out different is the Tzimisce joining the Camarilla in the Tremere's place. The whole reason the Elders of Clan Tzimisce didn't join (aside from their independent streak, of course) is because the Tremere were founding members. The one hated the other, so occupying the same sect was never going to happen. If the Tremere become Liches, though, the Tzimisce have no beef with them. They didn't have their blood usurped. At worst, individual Voivodes might have beef with the Tremere, as competitors for arcane resources. But the Clan itself will likely not care.<br /> <br /> Obviously, due to the Omen Wars, the Tzimisce don't have a high opinion of the Ventrue either. But, especially in the face of their rebellious Childer, enough Tzimisce Elders/Methuselahs would be willing to tolerate the Blue Bloods enough to form an alliance of convenience. Though they would then spend the better part of a millennia going forward being rivals to the Ventrue within the Camarilla to the degree the Brujah normally are. Which would have the side-effect of preventing a single obvious trio of close-knit &quot;Pillar Clans&quot; from occupying the center of Camarilla unlife. Instead, you might see the Camarilla broken into a couple of major sides (Ventrue and Toreador here, Brujah and Tzimisce there, and Malkavian, Gangrel, and Nosferatu either forming their own block or just sitting as the buffer between the two groups).<br /> <br /> Also, the Banu Haqiim probably don't get saddled with the Tremere Curse, because the Tremere aren't involved in Kindred politics. Not unless the Tzimisce come together to inflict a Koldunic equivalent, which I don't see happening. Making the Assamites a more persistent threat down the centuries. Or at least the Web of Knives. (It's entirely possible, without the Tremere, the more moderate parts of the Banu Haqim - the Viziers and Sorcerers - elect to join the Camarilla. Granting the sect access to alternative sources of Blood Sorcery.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-30T19:32:44-07:00","id":1545085,"title":"","content":"One big change would be the general lack of Tzimisce in the Sabbat. The war between the Tzimisce and Tremere radically changed the Tzimisce. The older Tzimsice began mass embracing and bloodbonding younger vampires to send them off to war with the Tremere. If the Tremere weren't around, you wouldn't have seen anything like that, and you probably would not have seen the deal with Kupala, the Valdurie in the Sabbat, etc. You'd still see an Anarch revolt and the formation of a Sabbat, but the Lasombra would be the only real clan in it, and without the Valdurie, you'd see the Sabbat constantly fracturing and tearing itself apart. I can't imagine the Tzimsice would join the Camarilla, so they'd probably be an independent clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-30T23:37:12-07:00","id":1545088,"title":"","content":"On the mage end the order would probably be in a stronger position post massada war and the tremere probably would have been decimated. This creates a more potent force supporting the magical aspects of natural philosophy in early moderm period. Potentially slowing the rise of the order of reason.<br /> <br /> assuming the traditions didnt make any big gaffes and things genrally went as they did. Our tech may be 10-30 years behind but a lot more superstition and sorcerors are about","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-31T12:15:09-07:00","id":1545098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1545066-alt-history-tremere-becomes-liches?p=1545085#post1545085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One big change would be the general lack of Tzimisce in the Sabbat. The war between the Tzimisce and Tremere radically changed the Tzimisce. The older Tzimsice began mass embracing and bloodbonding younger vampires to send them off to war with the Tremere. If the Tremere weren't around, you wouldn't have seen anything like that, and you probably would not have seen the deal with Kupala, the Valdurie in the Sabbat, etc. You'd still see an Anarch revolt and the formation of a Sabbat, but the Lasombra would be the only real clan in it, and without the Valdurie, you'd see the Sabbat constantly fracturing and tearing itself apart. I can't imagine the Tzimsice would join the Camarilla, so they'd probably be an independent clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weren't the Tzimisce also mass-Embracing in response to the Omen Wars? I think they'd still have a ton of Fledglings to throw at that problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-31T21:00:38-07:00","id":1545120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1545066-alt-history-tremere-becomes-liches?p=1545098#post1545098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Weren't the Tzimisce also mass-Embracing in response to the Omen Wars? I think they'd still have a ton of Fledglings to throw at that problem.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The omen wars started between tzimisce and tremere, as the formers koldun predicted in omens that the fledgling tremere would lead to disaster for their clan. <br /> So no tremere clan, no omen wars, no mass embrace, at least for that<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-31T21:32:36-07:00","id":1545121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1545066-alt-history-tremere-becomes-liches?p=1545076#post1545076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. Assamites would never have been cursed after being defeated, probably leading to the extinction of the clan or decimation down to a bloodline population.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the older books (Assamite revised clanbook?) said that the Tremere were pushing for the Assamites to be extinguished outright, and that their Curse was a compromise. So it's likely that whatever more moderate voices were advocating for lesser punishment would have won out, although it's possible they might not have respected the Camarilla's strength as much as they had in the canon timeline and, with their bloodthirst unrestrained by fancy magic, done other stupid things later that got them in trouble.<br /> <br /> A lot fewer antitribu at the least, though, if any. Hell, maybe ur-Shulgi never wakes up at all (best timeline).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2218-ideon","name":"Ideon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-01T03:19:38-07:00","id":1545128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ideon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1545066-alt-history-tremere-becomes-liches?p=1545121#post1545121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the older books (Assamite revised clanbook?) said that the Tremere were pushing for the Assamites to be extinguished outright, and that their Curse was a compromise. So it's likely that whatever more moderate voices were advocating for lesser punishment would have won out, although it's possible they might not have respected the Camarilla's strength as much as they had in the canon timeline and, with their bloodthirst unrestrained by fancy magic, done other stupid things later that got them in trouble.<br /> <br /> A lot fewer antitribu at the least, though, if any. Hell, maybe ur-Shulgi never wakes up at all (best timeline).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of those things that sound great initially and then make less sense the more you think about it. If the vampire society in general decided that the Assamites needed a spanking, once they were banging down the doors of Alamut, there isn't really a good reason to stop just short of completing the goal.<br /> <br /> As for the Tremere being the voice advocating for extermination, this makes less sense because any Clan with Auspex as a clan discipline is automatically less at risk than those without being able to counter Obfuscate. But when you consider the safety level of Thaumaturgical Wards provide when stacked with access to Auspex, then there is little to no reason why the Tremere would have a hardon for exterminating the Assamites in the first place.<br /> <br /> Then again when the lore was written that the Tremere placed the curse on the Assamites, the Tremere were the only magic users among the undead. I doubt they would have allowed the Vizirs of the Assamites to stay intact and retain their libraries of mystical knowledge. Likewise, it is unclear how the Assamites were able to develop a Generation lowering vitae potion technology which didn't require the consumption of a soul, but somehow the clan of vampire mages never went down this particular path of research or demanded it be turned over as part of the ongoing punishment against the assamite clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-01T23:31:40-07:00","id":1545197,"title":"","content":"Loving this topic, it's terrific food for thought.<br /> <br /> Taking the &quot;Tzimisce join the Camarilla&quot; ball and running with it, the impact that this has on the culture of the Sabbat is colossal. Aside from a significant minority of Tzimisce Antitribu, the sect develops over the following centuries without having to reluctantly accept as an equal the clan that does the most to uplift the vampiric condition as a form of posthuman transcendence. Clan Lasombra's closest allies are Spanish Brujah and the Black Hand's Banu Haqim.<br /> <br /> The Path of Blood, the Path of Caine, and the Path of Power and the Inner Voice still figure prominently in Sabbat culture, but the Camarilla aren't championing Humanity to the exclusion of all other ethoi as long as there are Metamorphosists in the Inner Circle. Paths might be a phenomenon that survives the Dark Ages to become the norm in the Final Nights, with Gangrel, Tzimisce, and Ventrue following the Paths of the Beast, of Death and the Soul, and of Honorable Accord openly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 11-02-2024, 02:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-01T23:54:52-07:00","id":1545199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1545066-alt-history-tremere-becomes-liches?p=1545197#post1545197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paths might be a phenomenon that survives the Dark Ages to become the norm in the Final Nights, with Gangrel, Tzimisce, and Ventrue following the Paths of the Beast, of Death and the Soul, and of Honorable Accord openly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the <b>Via Venator Umbra</b> would survive and would become the de-facto default path for many. With &quot;sins&quot; ike &quot;Not defending your territory.&quot;, &quot;Avoiding contact with civilization.&quot; and &quot;Failing to offer hospitality to an invited (or announced) visitor.&quot; the Tzimisce would morph the Camarilla into something very Voivodate-like just on the global scale and the Ventrue would jump in gleafully<br /> The Ashirra and the Sabbat, not to mention the basically non-existant Anarch would have a really hard time to gain foothold<br /> But I think the Sabbat would be formed around the Lasombra - Salubri - Cappadocian triumvirate and Faith and the Church would be their primary area of influence - even if the Antediluvians survive - they wouldn't really be the sword of Caine but the Sword of Abel, a counter-balance to the Camarilla, a bit like Church vs State, that Sabbat would be a bit like the <b>Raktasadhu of India</b> not the howling monsters of the night\u200b with very different goals","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-04T00:03:22-08:00","id":1545281,"title":"","content":"I'm not the closest follower of M:tA lore, but I'm curious to hear anyone's thoughts on how House Tremere itself fares in this alternate history. They're persona non grata within the Order of Hermes, surely, breaking away under a cloud of mutual animosity between themselves and the other houses within the Order. How do the Tremere get by without the Camarilla to insinuate themselves into? Do they remain active players in the Ascension War? Do they tip the balance against the Technocracy or any of the setting's other metaplot villains? Do they spend the centuries exploring other realms and territories in search of a cure to their new condition or a new purpose to while away eternity? Without the diablerie of Saulot hanging around House Tremere's necks like an albatross, does the Tal'mahe'ra ever flirt with recruiting them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-05T09:24:57-08:00","id":1545391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1545066-alt-history-tremere-becomes-liches?p=1545281#post1545281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not the closest follower of M:tA lore, but I'm curious to hear anyone's thoughts on how House Tremere itself fares in this alternate history. They're persona non grata within the Order of Hermes, surely, breaking away under a cloud of mutual animosity between themselves and the other houses within the Order. How do the Tremere get by without the Camarilla to insinuate themselves into?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Order of Hermes has a hard stance against becoming undead. And, while the House it's one of the most powerful of the Order, if they were to face the whole Order in conflict they would loose because they wouldn't have the biggest advantage of being a vampire: easily renewable numbers.<br /> <br /> Probably the best ploy for the Tremere would be to try to keep things under wrapp for as long as possible. The more Liches can out-live the rest of the Order, the more magical power they can amass, to potentially get an edge over the rest of the Order.<br /> <br /> Truth be told, they tried to fool the order as vampires. And that worked surprisingly well, but not well enough to avoid the Massa War forever. However, lichdoom may be easier to hidde than vampirism. They can still use Sphere magick, so they can still do rituals with other wizards and produce results. No need to hidde in Transilvania and reject all contact<br /> <br /> If I remember correctly using spying magick against members of the Order - while widely practiced - it's also forbidden. That being the case, one can't complain against people hidding their auras and stuff - you shouldn't be prying the secrets of other mages in the first place. I imagine this law is a good part of why the Tremere were able to hidde their vampirism fo so long as they did.<br /> <br /> So, I would say that there's a non-zero (but admitedly low) chance that there could be a House Tremere with an undead conspiracy inside the OoH for a long time, perhaps even to the modern nigths. If the Tremere manage to retain influence for long enough, they may try to soften the Order views about undeath, but if the Traditions ever form that becomes more unlikely because it would cause a lot of friction with the rest of them (most notably with the Euthanatos). It could be a very dark secret of the Order, waiting to be blown up<br /> <br /> If they get discovered early, I don't see the Tremere liches surviving (one could, perhaps, draw a paralel with the Ars Magica timeline?). The longer it takes for the OoE/Traditions to unveil the secret, the more likely the upper echelons of the Tremere could become powerful enough to escape consequences<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do they remain active players in the Ascension War? Do they tip the balance against the Technocracy or any of the setting's other metaplot villains? </div> </div> </div>This one it's interesting because the Tremere caused a whole lot of problems on their attempt to survive the OoH and the Omen War.<br /> <br /> Most notably, the event that jumpstarted the Ascencion War was the fall of Mistridge (a chantry of very evil Hermetics) at the hand of the rebel Craftmasons. Unbeknownst to most, this victory of the young masons was made possible by a Tremere (Goroatrix?) lowering the defenses from the inside. The Tremere were blammed mostly because it happened after the start of the Massa War, and thus the Massons escaped consequences, and eventually grew to become the founders of the Order of Reason(Technocracy).<br /> <br /> If the Tremere get exposed before the Masons muster the guts to rebel and put MIstridge to the cannon (arround 1210), they could try to resort to the same tactic of opening more fronts of war for the OoH. But they are going to end defeated. Maybe the most powerful (like Tremere himself) could flee, but their influence stops there and most of Mage remains all the same<br /> <br /> BUT if the Tremere managed to stay hidden within the Order a few decades more, this wouldn't have happened. The masons would most likely have been defeated w/o Tremere help. Even if the Tremere still consider causing trouble for the Order it's a good idea, they wouldn't be able to take the blunt of the OoH response to give the Masons time to grow - then the Masons would've been pursued and executed.<br /> <br /> If the Masons fail, the OoR doesn't exist as we know it, the Ascencon War could have a completely different face<br /> <br /> It's possible we would have a more fragmented scenario:<br /> <br /> The mirriad of technomancers that formed the Order of Reason still exist, and it's still likely they would find common ground at some point (this ain't even the first time technomancers unify). But the &quot;pro-human&quot; and &quot;anti-supernatural&quot; approach has a lot to do with the justified hatred the Craftmasons had for the abuses of mages (of the OoH) over the masses. W/o the masons as founders, it's possible the &quot;Technocracy&quot; would have taken a far less militant approach against the supernatural. At the same time, it's more unlikely they would've sided with the Gabrielites (extremist christian witch-hunting mages)<br /> <br /> The Inquisition it's still happening, so the Gabrielites are still there with the torch of &quot;killing the supernatural&quot;, but w/o the OoR they have a lot less backing to do their thing. <br /> <br /> If the OoR doesn't surge as a power cappable (and willing) of toppling all fellowships, then the Traditions wouldn't form either as we know them (as they're largely a response of the formation of the Technocracy).<br /> <br /> An OoH that would be much stronger, w/o the Massa War and the Order of Reason depleting their resources (and perhaps having one extra house that happen to be excelent manipulators and also an undead-ruled conspiracy). They would most likely refuse any sort of alliance that doesn't place them at the top. In the face of inquisitorial mages, some small european factions could end being forced to join the OoH, or could decide to never leave (like the Bojnaer House that defected to the Verbena)<br /> <br /> Forces that want a unified faction of mystical practices do exist on the Batini. And as the world becomes more of a &quot;global town&quot;, somthing akin to the Traditions could form. Perhaps more akin to the newer Disparate Alliance<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do they spend the centuries exploring other realms and territories in search of a cure to their new condition or a new purpose to while away eternity? Without the diablerie of Saulot hanging around House Tremere's necks like an albatross, does the Tal'mahe'ra ever flirt with recruiting them? </div> </div> </div>Well, Tal'mahe'ra has &quot;liches&quot;. In some of the material it's implied these are vampires, but I always liked better the idea of these being Mage liches (TBH has a lot of crossover anyway)<br /> <br /> A recruitment from the Tal'mahe'ra could be an interesting development if the Tremere Liches get discovered, and have to flee the OoH<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-09T16:50:54-08:00","id":1545630,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of the Tzimisce being in the Camarilla. In fact, I\u2019ve made threads about it in the past. In this scenario, I think it makes sense because with no Tremere Clan, there is no Omen War. The Omen War destabilized the Tzimisce Clan which lead to them falling to their own Anarchs. <br /> <br /> Assuming the Lasombra still overthrow their elders, the Anarch Revolt still happens with the Lasombra in charge. The Tzimisce, being super-conservative and ruled by their elders, of course has to take an active hand in opposing the Anarchs and so becomes a leading force in what will become the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Would another Clan join the Sabbat? There isn\u2019t necessarily a reason for them to, but it might be interesting to maintain the 7 vs 2 balance. Maybe the Brujah should join the Anarch Revolt in larger numbers. It makes sense for them.<br /> <br /> The Tzimisce have an influence on the Camarilla - they are harsher, crueler, less human, more traditional. Maybe it is the Ventrue who become the more liberal rivals to the Tzimisce\u2019s conservatism. <br /> <br /> The Brujah are gone from the Camarilla now. Who replaces them? The Salubri perhaps?<br /> <br /> The Assamites still do their thing and are eventually defeated. Instead of being cursed by the Tremere, they are instead cursed by the Tzimisce - a curse that may involve Vicissitude and/or Koldunic Sorcery. This curse could be like the original: prohibiting them from drinking vampire blood, or it could be entirely different. <br /> <br /> So, the Camarilla:<br /> Tzimisce<br /> Ventrue<br /> Toreador<br /> Nosferatu<br /> Malkavian<br /> Gangrel<br /> Salubri?<br /> <br /> And the Sabbat:<br /> Lasombra<br /> Brujah","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-10T16:45:05-08:00","id":1545662,"title":"","content":"Here are a few other things to consider:<br /> <br /> It is often theorized that Tremere\u2019s Diablerie of Saulot and destruction of the Salubri Clan was actually planned by Saulot himself. If those theories are true, then Saulot would likely turn elsewhere instead of Tremere.<br /> <br /> Where would he turn? Maybe the Baali. They were likely created by Saulot as well and perhaps the conflict between the Salubri and Baali was part of Saulot\u2019s plan. Maybe the next step is having the Baali destroy the Salubri and trick one of the Baali methuselahs to Diablerize him? Could the Baali rise to full Clan status as they eliminate the Salubri.<br /> <br /> Another possibility is Augustus Giovanni - who certainly wanted full Clan status and was ready to exterminate a Clan and commit Diablerie to do it. The Giovanni are so closely connected to the Cappadocians, this option may seem less likely.<br /> <br /> I guess which ever is cooler.<br /> <br /> <br /> Another question is what are the Sabbat like without the Tzimisce but the Brujah instead instead. the Vaulderie came from the Tzimisce, so that won\u2019t be a thing. Also, the extremely cruelty and inhumanity of the Sabbat, including the rituals, likely came from the Tzimisce influence as well. We might have a nicer versus of the Sabbat to go with a crueler Camarilla, so the difference in humanity between the Sects will be less pronounced. <br /> <br /> The Brujah are more ideologically driven and a Sabbat under their influenced might put a greater emphasis on freedom and on the rights of the young. This Sabbat may be closer to its Anarch roots. Maybe they would be larger but less organized.<br /> <br /> There maybe also be more of a rivalry between the Brujah and Lasombra than there was between the Tzimisce and Lasombra. The Lasombra still want one rulers, the Brujah push for more rights and equality.<br /> <br /> There will be no Blood Brothers or an equivalent. There will be no war ghouls - except maybe rarely used by the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat will likely have a number of other noteworthy cultural and institutional differences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-11T01:14:41-08:00","id":1545677,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1129_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1129\" data-vbnamecard=\"1129\">Sergeant Brother</a> I think that the Tzimisce would be a split clan, with the Old Clan and Koldunic sorcerers residing in the Camarilla, while the Vicissitude users in the Sabbat. Thus, the Sabbat would be swimming in Szlachta servitors, but very few if any Vozhd.<br /> <br /> As for Saulot, it is a tricky thing to map out because you could just as easily argue that after waking up from his torpor, he marches back to the East to further expand his powers of Kuei-Jin disciplines. Imagine a whole army of Warrior Salubri being supported by Salubri Healers and lead by Wu-Zao scouts to lay siege against Yama King strongholds and Kuei-jin alike.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-11T09:59:10-08:00","id":1545702,"title":"","content":"I like the notion of Old Clan Tziscme and the Koldunic branch being part of the Camarilla and focused on there passions while the visscuitde users would be outcasts savages of the Sabbat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-11T13:13:23-08:00","id":1545705,"title":"","content":"So if the Tzimisce are split, where do the Revenant families end up? A lot of the prominent ones have Vicissitude, though the Camarilla is a lot more tolerant of ghouls than the Sabbat. Maybe the families would be with the Camarilla but wouldn\u2019t have Vicissitude. Maybe some went with the Sabbat and some with the Camarilla?<br /> <br /> On a different topic, would the rise of the Giovanni happen the same as in canon or would the lack of the Tremere cause a different reaction or a different chain of events regarding Augustus Giovanni.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-11T18:34:50-08:00","id":1545722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1545066-alt-history-tremere-becomes-liches?p=1545705#post1545705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a different topic, would the rise of the Giovanni happen the same as in canon or would the lack of the Tremere cause a different reaction or a different chain of events regarding Augustus Giovanni.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Augustus's ambitions would have changed without the Tremere. That feels like it was an inevitability that he would usurp Cappadocius.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6423-higgipedia","name":"higgipedia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-11T18:48:11-08:00","id":1545723,"title":"","content":"Augustus Giovanni was very ruthless and ambitious and it was that facet that made Japeth and his Childe Lady Constancia very wary of making him a member of the clan and especially a direct childe of Cappadocius.<br /> <br /> So sooner or later he would make a play to get rid of the competition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-11T23:08:49-08:00","id":1545729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1545066-alt-history-tremere-becomes-liches?p=1545705#post1545705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if the Tzimisce are split, where do the Revenant families end up? A lot of the prominent ones have Vicissitude, though the Camarilla is a lot more tolerant of ghouls than the Sabbat. Maybe the families would be with the Camarilla but wouldn\u2019t have Vicissitude. Maybe some went with the Sabbat and some with the Camarilla?</div> </div> </div> </div>My memory is a bit hazy on this, but last I checked the production of a Revenant bloodline didn't require vicissitude. So I could easily see a Revenant clan like the Ducheski working for the Kolduns rather than the Tremere in the Camarilla. The Old Clan Tzimisce would probably just consider a Revenant bloodline to be well bred servants who help maintain the masquerade. As you suggest, the Sabbat revenant lines would be the flesh crafted ones.<br /> <br /> On a related note, I have always felt that the Nosferatu would have some human and animal Revenant bloodlines because of their use of spawning pools on many generations of animals and the fact that the homeless people who live in their sewers are already isolated from society, usually lack any kind of records, and they can be raised from birth to believe whatever you want them to believe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-12T02:55:17-08:00","id":1545735,"title":"","content":"You are not wrong<br /> There are TONS of Ravenant lines that are not Tzimisce and don1t had any vicissitude involved during their creation<br /> <br /> <b>D'habi:</b> An ancient revenant family owned by the Baali bloodline - no comment here, demon worshippers<br /> <b>Enrathi:</b> A bloodline associated with the True Black Hand, infamous for abducting and training chatterlings (Chatterlings were mortal humans, abducted as children by the True Black Hand to be trained as servants and ghouls until they are deemed worthy of being Embraced.)<br /> <b>Kairouan Brotherhood: </b>A family created through experiments of Assamite Sorcerers<br /> <b>Katayama: </b>The youngest of the revenant families. the creation of Dr. Douglas Netchurch and his childe Dr. Nancy Reage.<br /> <b>Keskinen:</b> A revenant family that serves the ancient Malkavian Louhi.<br /> <b>Marijava: </b>A bloodline associated with the True Black Hand. While they are trained as thieves and assassins, their primary function is as spies.<br /> <b>Rafastio: </b>They are witches, sorcerers, and seers loosely affiliated with the True Black Hand. They primarily act as the sect's liaisons to the Verbena tradition. Most of the members study Magick and a few are actual Awakened mages.<br /> <b>Servants of Anushin-Rawan:</b> Debased fisher-folk who served an eccentric Ventrue in early modern Greece.<br /> <b>Rosselini:</b> The Rosselini family were once mortal necromancers that crossed paths with the Giovanni. Being &quot;persuaded&quot; to become a part of the family, the Rosselinis underwent an unknown necromantic ritual to be transformed into Revenants<br /> <b>Ducheski: </b>A family formerly named Krevcheski and owned by the Tzimisce that now serves the Tremere, they are known for their skill at magic and at making mechanical devices, particularly implements of torture. Many Tremere have the Ducheski maintain their libraries and laboratories.\u200b<br /> <br /> Also:<br /> <b>VTM: Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom, p. 15<br /> Zhenga</b> is a Setite who operates in the criminal underworld of Mombasa.<br /> <u><b>Biography:</b></u> Slaves, drugs, vitae, and secrets are all hers and for anyone to buy \u2013 for the right price. Standing on good ground with the native Laibon, Zhenga prepares to claim Mombasa as her official domain to serve as a beachhead for Setite operations in sub-Saharan Africa. <b>She is also trying to create a new revenant line called <i>bima</i></b> (the Nilote word for ghoul), obedient only to the Setites in the African wilderness. The &quot;bima project&quot; has enjoyed some few successes and the resulting revenants are dark and hairy, with long canine teeth and thick, clawlike fingernails.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-12T10:25:49-08:00","id":1545745,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the list ShadowProwler. I knew some of these families existed but not much else about them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-18T19:01:19-08:00","id":1546107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1545066-alt-history-tremere-becomes-liches?p=1545702#post1545702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the notion of Old Clan Tziscme and the Koldunic branch being part of the Camarilla and focused on there passions while the visscuitde users would be outcasts savages of the Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do like the idea of the Camarilla having the more traditional, &quot;Dracula-type&quot; Tzimisce. The ones lay people think about when they think of vampires. Aristocratic. Mind-controlling. Quasi-mystical.<br /> <br /> And then the flesh-crafters get shunted to this extremist sect, where they can practice and perfect their &quot;Art&quot; unrestrained by petty morality or the needs of the Masquerade (comparatively, anyway).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-21T23:48:40-08:00","id":1546275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1545066-alt-history-tremere-becomes-liches?p=1545662#post1545662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Brujah are more ideologically driven and a Sabbat under their influenced might put a greater emphasis on freedom and on the rights of the young. This Sabbat may be closer to its Anarch roots. Maybe they would be larger but less organized.<br /> <br /> There maybe also be more of a rivalry between the Brujah and Lasombra than there was between the Tzimisce and Lasombra. The Lasombra still want one rulers, the Brujah push for more rights and equality.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's notable that the Sabbat's Brujah have a history of antagonizing the Lasombra in the canon timeline, as well. Books set in the Final Nights don't seem to have ever picked that ball up and run with it, but the recognition of the Panders as a clan is supposed to have been the compromise that ended a Sabbat civil war between the Brujah and the joint leadership of the Lasombra and Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> This is almost a side tangent, but it's long been my headcanon that the Camarilla and Anarch Brujah are often less than completely sincere in their pursuit of egalitarianism. Infiltrating mortal social justice movements has been an effective way to get access to herds of kine that the other clans don't know how to talk to, but the Brujah of old were a High Clan. Rulership's been in their blood since Carthage, even if the Ventrue and Lasombra have been successful at opposing them since the nights of Rome. I imagine that jockeying for position continuing in our Alternate Universe Sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}